# Downloaded model archives (retrieved by tools/fetch_models.py; original licenses apply)
data/raw/
# Third-party mechanism SOURCES, extracted from those archives.
#
# Twelve of fourteen implementations are fetch-at-runtime: their upstream terms
# permit academic USE but grant no redistribution right to this project (see
# docs/ASSET_REDISTRIBUTION.md).  A public repository is redistribution, so the
# bytes must not be tracked -- 191 .mod and 2 .inc files were removed from the
# whole history on 2026-08-15, before the first push.
#
# What the repository distributes instead is data/provenance/downloads.json:
# URL, SHA-256, byte count and fetch timestamp per asset.  Run
# `python3 tools/fetch_models.py` to reconstruct this directory; it fails closed
# if any hash does not match, so a reader's tree is verifiably the tree the
# results were computed from.
data/models/*/mod/*.mod
data/models/*/mod/*.inc
# Compiled NEURON mechanism libraries (rebuilt by tools/build_mechanisms.py)
data/models/*/mod/arm64/
data/models/*/mod/x86_64/
data/models/*/mod/*.o
data/models/*/mod/*.c
# Simulation output (regenerated by tools/run_campaign.py)
results/features/
results/traces/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.ipynb_checkpoints/
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# Run-local, not release artifacts.
#
# `results/logs/` is the driver's per-stage stdout; `run_receipt.py` already
# treats it as unattributable and the release inventory does not declare it.
# `_superseded_run_*/` is what `run_all.sh --force` moves aside before a
# rebuild -- a snapshot of the PREVIOUS release, kept on disk so nothing is
# destroyed, and precisely the thing the manifest's orphan policy exists to
# keep out of the current one.
results/logs/
results/_superseded_run_*/
results/features/*/_superseded/

# macOS Finder metadata; never release content.
.DS_Store
